{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Gold and silver and copper.</b> He mentioned three kinds of metal and three kinds of wool, and we do not find silk in the donation of the Tabernacle, because it comes from the body of a creeping thing, which is the silkworm, and it was not deemed fit for the work of Heaven, but only something pure; as they said concerning the tahash and the dye of the crimson worm — it is not from the body of the worm but from grains within which the worm is found. Afterward he mentioned <b>and linen</b> (ושש), which is flax, and he mentioned <b>and goats</b> (ועזים), which is the wool. And this is why Onkelos did not translate ועזיא but rather ומעזי, which means a thing coming from the goats, namely the wool. And even though a garment of wool and linen the Torah forbade to us, the priests do not enter to serve in the Sanctuary except in wool and linen, and in the section Kodashim I shall explain the secret of the matter, with Heaven's help."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:47.618327773Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}